# TalentIQ

TalentIQ is an AI-powered workforce intelligence platform. Managers get
skill-based project recommendations, team formation, skill-gap analysis
and workload tracking; employees manage their skills, availability,
development roadmap and project progress.

## Project structure

- `frontend/` – React + Vite + Tailwind client
- `backend/` – FastAPI API, PostgreSQL (SQLAlchemy + Alembic), Neo4j skill graph
- `docs/` – project documentation and design notes

## Requirements

- Python 3.12
- Node.js 18+
- PostgreSQL 16
- Neo4j 5 (optional – only the Skill Gaps graph view needs it)

## Getting started

### 1. Backend

Create `backend/.env`:

```
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres:<password>@localhost:5432/talentiq_db
SECRET_KEY=<any long random string>
APP_NAME=TalentIQ
APP_VERSION=1.0.0
NEO4J_URI=bolt://127.0.0.1:7687
NEO4J_USERNAME=neo4j
NEO4J_PASSWORD=<neo4j password>
NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j
```

Create an empty `talentiq_db` database in PostgreSQL, then from `backend/`:

```
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
alembic upgrade head
python -m app.seed
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

The seed creates a manager (`manager@talentiq.dev`) and sample employees,
all with the password `Password123!`.

To load the skill graph into Neo4j (after Neo4j is running):

```
python -m scripts.sync_neo4j
```

### 2. Frontend

From `frontend/`:

```
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000. The API is expected at http://127.0.0.1:8000
(override with `VITE_API_URL`).

